      {
        "id": "b15fcabd-7609-4ab4-84e3-594daec3dec1",
        "date": "2026-07-02T04:14:19.701Z",
        "order": 10,
        "seriesId": "0908d142-9b5c-4aee-9701-57660ed4c60f",
        "ebookId": "f9fa53f6-6751-46df-885d-b4895668caf4",
        "ebook": {
          "id": "f9fa53f6-6751-46df-885d-b4895668caf4",
          "at": "tsukimichi-vol-9",
          "title": "Tsukimichi - Vol. 9",
          "subtitle": "Moonlit Fantasy",
          "description": "As chaos erupts in the hyuman world, a reluctant trump card is forced into play...\r\n\r\nUsing the commotion caused by Rotsgard’s mutant outbreak, the demon army makes its move—marching on the capitals of the Kingdom of Limia and Gritonia Empire.\r\n\r\nFaced with the four-armed demon general Io, the kingdom’s hero finds themselves cornered, without hope.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, Makoto is abducted yet again by the Goddess and coerced into assisting the hero in crisis.\r\n\r\nPushed around by both gods and demons alike, Makoto turns the tables with an unexpected counterstrategy!\r\n\r\nAs the battlefield descends into chaos, demons, hyumans, and the Demiplane each pursue their own agenda in a deadly clash of ambitions!",
